This file gathers and re-exports the choice-free recursion theory for computability in effectively given domains: the basic arithmetic and closure lemmas, the at-least-two and zero bits, decidability from a universal quantification and from unary, paired, and triple zero-one characteristics, recursive enumerability from a universal quantification, the length bound on a decoded list, exponentiation and its primitive recursiveness, halving and parity, division and remainder by two, maximum and the conditional, the bounded universal and existential deciders, the pair-map on coded lists, the parameterized bounded universal quantification of a recursively enumerable predicate over a decoded list, bitwise or, the list existential and universal characters, swapping a binary decidable relation, append of coded lists, the fuel table and its agreement with a course-of-values recursion, the fuel-ok decoder, the fuel-bounded state card and the matches characteristic, the code bound, and the nonempty, consistency, subset, and intersection-equality characters.
